0..71 Comment "// A function reads a module\'s signature as a value, and a model as its"
72..129 Comment "// entries at a type that the signature\'s value computes."
130..132 Comment "//"
133..207 Comment "// A render over a module reads both parts. The presentation of a `theory`"
208..282 Comment "// block is a `Theory` value, so an ordinary function folds a signature. A"
283..361 Comment "// model is a record at `Model(T)`. A generic render needs the model at a type"
362..439 Comment "// that it computes from the value, and an equivalence relates the two types."
440..442 Comment "//"
443..517 Comment "// `declared` folds `std.build`\'s `Gandr.Package` into eleven constants at"
518..595 Comment "// `String`. The members of the theories it includes come first, in the order"
596..673 Comment "// of its `include` lines. `toolchain` reads the content fields of a model by"
674..747 Comment "// their names. `std.build`\'s `modelType` computes the entries\' type of a"
748..822 Comment "// presentation, one entry for each constant. The maps between a package\'s"
823..898 Comment "// model and its entries, their two round trips and their equivalence check"
899..976 Comment "// here, beside those of the local theory `Flagged`, which has a string and a"
977..1052 Comment "// boolean constant. `encode` folds a presentation and its entries into one"
1053..1130 Comment "// line for each constant. `render` is that fold for a package\'s model, inert"
1131..1164 Comment "// because it reads inert fields."
1165..1167 Comment "//"
1168..1244 Comment "// Limits: an entry is a string, a boolean or opaque, and the render escapes"
1245..1323 Comment "// no character. The render writes one table in the order of the presentation,"
1324..1396 Comment "// where the manifest step writes three tables in its own order (#4725)."
1397..1399 Comment "//"
1400..1415 Comment "// - see: #4730"
1416..1431 Comment "// - see: #6046"
1432..1447 Comment "// - see: #6071"
1448..1540 Comment "// - see: `../../pathological/desc/module-reflection.gandr` — what does not reach a module"
